  "difficulty": "medium",
  "categories": ["monotonic-stack", "stack", "array"],
  "descriptionMd": "You are given `temperatures`, the daily temperature readings for a run of consecutive days.\n\nFor each day, work out how many days you would have to wait until a **strictly warmer** day arrives. If no warmer day ever comes, use `0` for that day. Return these waiting times as an array.\n\n**Example 1**\n\n```\ntemperatures = [73, 74, 75, 71, 69, 72, 76, 73]\n→ [1, 1, 4, 2, 1, 1, 0, 0]\n```\nAfter day 2 (75°) the next warmer reading is 76° on day 6, four days later.\n\n**Example 2**\n\n```\ntemperatures = [30, 40, 50, 60]\n→ [1, 1, 1, 0]\n```\n\n**Follow-up:** can you do it in O(n) time?",
  "constraints": ["1 ≤ temperatures.length ≤ 10⁵", "30 ≤ temperatures[i] ≤ 100"],
  "hints": ["Keep track of the days that are still waiting for a warmer day. What do their temperatures look like, in order?", "When a new day arrives, it resolves every waiting day that is colder than it — and those are always the most recently added ones."],
  "signature": {
    "functionName": "dailyTemperatures",
    "params": [{ "name": "temperatures", "type": "int[]" }],
    "returns": "int[]"
  },
